            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 20,
              "start": 20
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "According to Justice Scalia, justice Scalia questioned whether fees are assessable when the only victory is procedural."
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Justice Breyer",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "dcda670d3683c788004cd1fae808688d561770bcfbacb55f1d32322a6c979e53",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-dcda670d3683-0001-0002"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 22,
              "start": 22
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "Justice Breyer asked whether a party who wins only a technical hearing should receive attorney\u2019s fees."
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Chief Justice Roberts",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "dcda670d3683c788004cd1fae808688d561770bcfbacb55f1d32322a6c979e53",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-dcda670d3683-0001-0003"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 23,
              "start": 23
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "According to Chief Justice Roberts, chief Justice Roberts wondered about a scenario where a plaintiff wins every procedural issue but ultimately loses on the merits."
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Justice Stevens",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "dcda670d3683c788004cd1fae808688d561770bcfbacb55f1d32322a6c979e53",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-dcda670d3683-0001-0004"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 24,
              "start": 24
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "Justice Stevens asked whether treating the statute as having a prevailing\u2011party clause is appropriate."
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Justice Breyer",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "dcda670d3683c788004cd1fae808688d561770bcfbacb55f1d32322a6c979e53",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-dcda670d3683-0001-0006"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 37,
              "start": 37
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "According to Justice Breyer, justice Breyer later questioned the discretion of district judges to award fees when the plaintiff obtains some benefit."
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Justice Ginsburg",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "dcda670d3683c788004cd1fae808688d561770bcfbacb55f1d32322a6c979e53",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-dcda670d3683-0002-0000"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 38,
              "start": 38
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "According to Justice Ginsburg, justice Ginsburg posed a hypothetical about entitlement to documents in an interlocutory order."
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Justice Sotomayor",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "dcda670d3683c788004cd1fae808688d561770bcfbacb55f1d32322a6c979e53",
            "evidence_ids": [
